@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Real-World Azure DevOps Project";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="lead text-center">A step-by-step guide to implementing a real-world project using Azure DevOps with CI/CD, security best practices, and infrastructure automation.</p>
    <hr />

    <!-- Project Overview -->
    <div class="mt-4">
        <h2 class="text-success">Project Overview</h2>
        <p>
            This project demonstrates the end-to-end DevOps process for deploying a web application using Azure DevOps.
            It includes setting up repositories, implementing CI/CD pipelines, infrastructure automation, security enhancements, and monitoring.
        </p>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Application Type:</strong> .NET Core Web App with React Frontend</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Source Control:</strong> Azure Repos (Git)</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Build & Release:</strong> Azure Pipelines</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Infrastructure:</strong> Azure App Services with Terraform</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Security:</strong> RBAC & Secure Code Analysis</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Monitoring:</strong> Azure Monitor & Log Analytics</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/project-overview.jpg" alt="Project Overview" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Overview of our Real-World Azure DevOps Project</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- CI/CD Pipeline Setup -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-warning">Setting Up CI/CD Pipeline</h2>
        <p>
            The CI/CD pipeline automates code integration, testing, and deployment. It consists of:
        </p>
        <ol class="list-group list-group-numbered">
            <li class="list-group-item">Creating an Azure DevOps Repository and enabling branch policies.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Setting up a Build Pipeline (YAML) for automated testing and artifact creation.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Configuring a Release Pipeline for deploying the application to Azure.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Implementing Approvals and Gates for controlled deployments.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/cicd-pipeline.jpg" alt="CI/CD Pipeline" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>CI/CD Pipeline Implementation in Azure DevOps</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Infrastructure as Code -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-danger">Infrastructure as Code (IaC)</h2>
        <p>
            Infrastructure is provisioned using Terraform, ensuring consistency and automation.
            The Terraform configuration includes:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Azure Resource Group</strong> for organizing resources.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Azure App Service</strong> for hosting the web application.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Azure SQL Database</strong> for storing application data.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Terraform Backend</strong> using Azure Storage.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/terraform-iac.jpg" alt="Terraform Infrastructure" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Infrastructure as Code with Terraform</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Security Best Practices -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-info">Security Best Practices</h2>
        <p>
            Security is integrated throughout the DevOps process:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Role-Based Access Control (RBAC):</strong> Restrict access to Azure resources.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Secure Code Analysis:</strong> Implement static code analysis in pipelines.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Secrets Management:</strong> Store sensitive data in Azure Key Vault.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Continuous Compliance Checks:</strong> Use Azure Policy to enforce security rules.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/security-devops.jpg" alt="Security in DevOps" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Security Measures in Azure DevOps</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Monitoring and Logging -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-secondary">Monitoring and Logging</h2>
        <p>
            Azure Monitor and Log Analytics provide insights into application performance and security logs.
            Key features include:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Azure Monitor:</strong> Collect and analyze telemetry data.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Application Insights:</strong> Monitor application health and detect issues.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Log Analytics:</strong> Query logs for security and performance monitoring.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Alerts:</strong> Set up notifications for critical events.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/azure-monitor.jpg" alt="Azure Monitoring" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Real-time Monitoring with Azure</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Conclusion -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-dark">Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
            This real-world project showcases a complete Azure DevOps implementation, covering CI/CD, Infrastructure as Code,
            Security Best Practices, and Monitoring. By following these steps, teams can achieve an efficient, secure, and automated development lifecycle.
        </p>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/conclusion.jpg" alt="DevOps Implementation Summary" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>End-to-End Azure DevOps Implementation</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
